e GPL or the mozilla license if  you like so just at the end this is  where it gets social this is the awkward  posthumous talk because it would be  almost dishonest of me not to address  what might well be considered the  elephant in the room at this point  because you only that our community  leaders sometimes turn out to be a bit  rubbish and Richard as it happens  Richard Stallman it's not necessary an  exception to this I don't think he's  actually malicious in any real sense but  the truth is is  it says some pretty awful things I don't  think he means to hurt people but it's  more a matter of not knowing quite how  to behave properly in civilized society  and I mean I don't mean to excuse him  actually it is a bit problematic for the  leader of the free software movement to  to behave in this way and maybe it's  time for him to step down and when it  comes to Eric Raymond I'm not even going  to go that he's literally the worst  person in existence I just feel it's  important to mention that and my purpose  in going to this rather dark place at  the end of the talk is to stress that  even though the idea of open-source been  always have sort of sprung from the most  saintly of people it's not about the  people in the and we shouldn't be  treating these people as heroes which  not really treating anybody as heroes  and what matters is the idea of open  source or whichever direction you  approach it from whether it is from the  left or from the right or permissive  restrictive care or don't care  all of that it's not about the people  it's about the idea and the idea what it  comes down to in the end is the  knowledge embedded in the community  that's what's so important to protect  the knowledge of how to write software  and more broadly the knowledge of how to  do anything we as humans are able to do  even one day you and me we're going to  go to the stars and the knowledge to do  that we must preserve that at all costs  and that is what open source is really  all about thank you so much for enduring  this enjoy the book  you
 

